 "title": "Persons of interest",
 "hook": "OpenSanctions, an open-source project that launched its website last week, is “an international database of persons and companies of political, criminal, or economic interest.” It combines and standardizes data from 20+ sources, such as the US Treasury’s sanctions lists (DIP 2018.02.21), Interpol’s Red Notices, members of EU parliament, and the CIA’s index of world leaders.",
